# Copy to the front-end's .dockerignore AND .gcloudignore (same content).
# Cloud Build uploads what .gcloudignore lets through (the tarball stays in the
# project's <project>_cloudbuild bucket), then docker build filters by
# .dockerignore. The secret patterns mean the same in both syntaxes (`**/` = any
# depth, a leading `/` = this folder only); plain names like `.git` match only at
# the top in .dockerignore but at any depth in .gcloudignore, which is harmless.

# --- Secrets: never in a build context (SKILL.md rule 8) ----------------------
# The build stage runs `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is uploaded and
# copied. Front-end config is injected at container start (config.js), so no
# .env file is needed for the build.
**/.env*
**/.config
/vars
# For a front-end that lives at the repo root: keep the back-end (its
# .env_pydantic and vars/) out too. Harmless when there is no such folder.
/back-end

# --- Not part of the build ----------------------------------------------------
node_modules
dist
.git
# Local agent and tool state
.claude
.gstack
.remember
.superpowers
.playwright-mcp
